The development\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\~ (1) I have been deliberately using \u8220?discourse\u8221? and \u8220?discursiveness\u8221? instead of \u8220?dialectic\u8221? (a term, incidentally, that Hegel uses sparsely in the Logic) in an attempt to demystify the latter term. But it should be clear that the meaning is the same.{\ul
}{\super
81} Now, taken precisely \u8220?in becoming,\u8221? being can first be determined as what it is rhapsodically, that is, qualitatively, in one \u8220?what,\u8221? then in another, and so on, each \u8220?what\u8221? never constituting anything definitive. The logical problem is to hold these \u8220?whats\u8221? together, to make a discourse of them \u8211? in effect, to give a first, better delineated definition of the unity which is possible in becoming. Here is where Hegel makes several conceptual moves, introducing among others the concepts of \u8220?finitude,\u8221? \u8220?limitation,\u8221? and \u8220?infinity.\u8221? With this last, with \u8220?infinity,\u8221? a turning point is reached. As conceived by Hegel, the \u8220?infinite\u8221? is being inasmuch as, in being whatever it is (and this could be an indefinite series of \u8220?whats\u8221? \u8211? a \u8220?bad infinite,\u8221? as Hegel calls it), it remains by itself, or is now definable, in Hegel's terminology, as \u8220?being-for-itself.\u8221? The turn consists in the fact that, from now on, the conceptual stress is no longer on \u8220?what\u8221? a being happens to be but on its retaining unity (in its abiding with itself) regardless of what it might otherwise be as a \u8220?what.\u8221? This \u8220?abiding with itself\u8221? can of course acquire both the meaning of \u8220?continuity\u8221? and \u8220?discreteness.\u8221? The further move from the categories of \u8220?quality\u8221? to those of \u8220?quantity\u8221? is thereby secured. Even though our most elementary talk about things is unreflectively carried out in qualitative terms, the truth of that discourse, or the more determinate concept of the being which is its subject matter, is defined by the categories of \u8220?quantity.\u8221? (2) These categories divide into \u8220?quantity\u8221? as such, \u8220?quantum,\u8221? and \u8220?measure.\u8221? As quantified, being is said to be constituted of parts that can be taken as both continuous and discrete, and there is in principle no end to how many such parts can be generated by reflection. These parts are \u8220?quanta.\u8221? Now, something analogous was also already said of being as qualitatively determined, except that instead of \u8220?{\i
quanta}\u8221? one had to speak of \u8220?{\i
qualia},\u8221? of \u8220?whats.\u8221? The play between quantitative parts which, as such, can both run into one another and yet also fall apart, was also {\ul
}already played out in terms of the \u8220?some\u8221? and the \u8220?some other,\u8221? the \u8220?one\u8221? and the \u8220?many,\u8221? their reciprocal connection ultimately one of \u8220?attraction\u8221? and \u8220?repulsion.\u8221? It was precisely this qualitative play that made possible the transition to \u8220?quantity.\u8221? But the difference is that what counts most in \u8220?quantity\u8221? for the determination of a being is the {\i
rule} by which this play is carried out. True: the \u8220?quanta\u8221? that make up that being, inasmuch as they are taken as single terms subject to external calculation, still have to be qualitatively determined in order to be individually picked out for the calculation. That is to say, they must be immediately presupposed. As thus presupposed, however, they are from the start already in principle relegated \u8211? to anticipate now a category that comes into its own only as a result of the dialectic of \u8220?quantity\u8221? \u8211? to the \u8220?unessential.\u8221? Only as implicated in a referential play of terms carried out according to a rule, and deriving their magnitude from this play, do they denote the new unity of formal determination that \u8220?being\u8221? has now acquired. Progress in the development of quantity is measured precisely by the extent that the rules determining the play, rather than just presupposing its terms globally and/or singly, also determine the range within which they can enter into that play, to the point that the play itself generates the terms that enter into it. Such are the mathematical ratios. Hegel takes them in order: direct ratio, {\i
y}/{\i
x} = {\i
k}; inverse ratio, {\i
xy} = {\i
k}; and the ratio of powers, {\i
x}{\super
2} or {\i
