{\ql
C. Reciprocity of action\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\~ In finite causality it is substances that actively relate to each other. {\i
Mechanism} consists in this {\i
externality} of causality, where the cause's {\i
reflection} in its effect {\i
into itself} is at the same time a repelling {\i
being}, or where, in the {\i
self-identity} which the causal substance has in its effect, the substance is equally immediately {\i
external} to itself and the effect is {\i
transposed into another substance}. In reciprocity of action this mechanism is now sublated, for it contains {\i
first} the {\i
disappearing} of that original {\i
persistence} of {\i
immediate} substantiality; {\i
second}, the {\i
coming to be} of the {\i
cause}, and hence {\i
originariness} {\i
mediating} itself with itself through its {\i
negation}. At first, the reciprocity of action takes on the form of a reciprocal causality of {\i
substances} that are {\i
presupposed} and that {\i
condition each other}; each is with respect to the other {\i
both} active {\i
and} passive {\i
substance}. Since the two are thus passive and active at once, their difference is thereby already sublated; it is a totally transparent reflective shine; they are substances only in being the identity of the active and the passive. The reciprocity of action is itself, therefore, only a still {\i
empty way and manner}, and all that is still needed is merely the external 11.408bringing together of what is already there, both {\i
in itself} and as {\i
posited}. First of all, it is no longer {\i
substrates} that are referred to each other but substances; in the movement of conditional causality, the still left over {\i
presupposed immediacy} has been sublated, and {\i
what conditions} the causing activity is only {\i
an influence}, or {\i
its own passivity}. But this influence, moreover, does not come from {\i
another} substance originating it but from precisely a causality which is conditioned by influence, or one which is {\i
mediated}. This at first {\i
external factor} that accrues to the cause and constitutes the side of its passivity is therefore mediated {\i
through the causality itself}, is produced through its own activity and is, consequently, a {\i
passivity posited by its own very activity}. \u8211? Causality is conditioned and conditioning. As {\i
conditioning}, it is {\i
passive}; but it is equally so as {\i
conditioned}. This conditioning or passivity is the {\i
negation} of the cause through itself in {\ul
}that it makes itself essentially into an {\i
effect} and is cause precisely for that reason. {\i
Reciprocity of action} is, therefore, only causality itself; the cause does not just {\i
have} an effect but, in the effect, refers {\i
as cause} back to itself. Causality has thereby returned to {\i
its absolute concept} and has at the same time attained the {\i
concept} itself. At first, it is real necessity, absolute self-identity in which the difference between it and the determinations referring to each other within it are substances, {\i
free actualities}, over against one another. Necessity is in this way {\i
inner identity}; causality is the manifestation of it in which its reflective shine {\i
of substantial otherness} has been sublated, and necessity is elevated to {\i
freedom}. \u8211? In the reciprocity of action, originative causality displays itself as {\i
arising} from its negation, from passivity, and as {\i
passing away} into it, as a {\i
becoming}, but in such a way that this becoming is at the same time equally only {\i
shining}; the transition into {\i
otherness} is reflection-into-itself; {\i
negation}, which is the ground of the cause, is its positive {\i
rejoining} with itself. In the reciprocity of action, therefore, necessity and causality have disappeared; they contain both the {\i
immediate identity} as {\i
combination} and {\i
reference} and the {\i
absolute substantiality of the differences}, consequently their {\i
contingency}, the original {\i
unity} of substantial {\i
difference} and therefore the absolute contradiction. Necessity is being, {\i
because} being is; it is the unity of being with itself that has itself as {\i
ground}, but, conversely, because this being has a ground, it is not being; it is simply and solely {\i
reflective shining}, {\i
reference} or {\i
mediation}. Causality is this {\i
posited} transition of original being, of {\i
cause}, into reflective shine or mere {\i
positedness}, and, 11.409conversely, of positedness into originariness; but the {\i
identity itself} of being and reflective shine still is the {\i
inner} necessity. This {\i
inwardness} or this in-itself sublates the movement of causality; the result is that the substantiality of the sides that stand in relation is lost, and necessity unveils itself. Necessity does not come to be {\i
freedom} by vanishing but in that its still only {\i
inner} identity is {\i
manifested}, and this manifestation is the identical movement immanent to the different sides, the immanent reflection of shine as shine. \u8211? Conversely, {\i
contingency} thereby comes to be {\i
freedom} at the same time, for the sides of necessity, which have the shape of independent, free actualities that do not reflectively shine into each other, {\i
are now posited as an identity}, so that now these totalities of immanent reflection, in their differences, also {\i
shine as identical}, in other words, they are also posited as only one and the same reflection. No longer, therefore, does absolute substance as self-differentiating absolute form repel itself as necessity from itself, nor does it fall apart as {\i
contingency} into indifferent, external substances, but, on the contrary, it {\ul
}{\i
differentiates} itself: {\i
on the one hand}, into the totality (the heretofore passive substance) which is at the origin, as the reflection from internal determinateness, as simple whole that contains its {\i
positedness} within itself and {\i
in this positedness is posited as self-identical} \u8211? this is {\i
the universal} \u8211?; {\i
on the other hand}, into the totality (the hitherto causal substance) which is the reflection, equally from internal determinateness, into the negative determinateness which, just as the {\i
self-identical determinateness}, equally is the whole, but posited as the {\i
self-identical negativity} \u8211? the singular. But, because the {\i
universal} is self-identical only in that the {\i
determinateness} that it holds within is {\i
sublated}, hence it is the negative as negative, it immediately is {\i
the same negativity} that {\i
singularity} is. And the singularity, because it equally is the determinedly determined, the negative as negative, immediately is {\i
the same identity} that {\i
universality} is. This, their {\i
simple} identity, is the {\i
particularity} that, from the singular, holds the moment of {\i
determinateness}; from the universal, that of immanent {\i
reflection} \u8211? the two in immediate unity. These three totalities are therefore one and the same reflection that, as {\i
negative self-reference}, differentiates itself into the other two totalities \u8211? but as into a {\i
perfectly transparent difference}, namely into the {\i
determinate simplicity}, or into the {\i
simple determinateness}, which is their one same identity. \u8211? This is the {\i
concept}, the realm of {\i
subjectivity} or of {\i
freedom}. {\ql
