implicit}; on account of the self-subsistent diversity of the two sides of judgment, their {\i
posited} connection also has {\ul
}the two at first as diverse. But it is the {\i
identity void of difference} that in fact constitutes the {\i
true} connection of the subject and predicate. The determination of the concept is itself essentially a {\i
connection}, for it is a {\i
universal}; the same determinations, therefore, which the subject and the predicate each have, are also had by their connection. The connection is {\i
universal}, for it is the positive identity of both, of the subject and predicate; but it is also {\i
determinate}, for the determinateness of the predicate is the determinateness of the subject; it is {\i
singular} as well, for in it the self-subsisting extremes are sublated as in their negative unity. \u8211? In judgment, however, this identity is not posited yet; the copula is as the still indeterminate connection of being in general, \u8220?A {\i
is} B,\u8221? for the self-subsistence of the concept's determinacies, or the extremes, is in judgment the {\i
reality} that the concept has within. If the \u8220?is\u8221? of the copula were already {\i
posited} as the 12.59determinate and fulfilled {\i
